WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.177 --> 00:00:01.886
[Negan]
<i>Previously on</i> Dead City.

2
00:00:01.911 --> 00:00:05.212
[The Croat] <i>With the methane.
we can bring the city back.</i>

3
00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:06.397
[Negan] <i>Right around the time</i>

4
00:00:06.422 --> 00:00:08.413
<i>that the world turned into
shit soup.</i>

5
00:00:08.438 --> 00:00:10.745
<i>The Croat showed up at my door.</i>

6
00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:13.672
<i>Said that I made him feel safe.</i>

7
00:00:14.001 --> 00:00:16.090
[Dama]
<i>He murdered your husband.</i>

8
00:00:16.115 --> 00:00:17.435
-[Negan grunts]
-[Maggie grunts]

9
00:00:19.074 --> 00:00:21.873
Just look after Ginny. will ya?

10
00:00:21.898 --> 00:00:23.160
No!

11
00:00:23.185 --> 00:00:25.317
[Dama] <i>Our world
has been destroyed.</i>

12
00:00:26.054 --> 00:00:28.491
<i>So now. we get
to build something new.</i>

13
00:00:31.553 --> 00:00:37.515
[eerie music]

14
00:00:45.132 --> 00:00:46.872
[hammer pounding]

15
00:00:47.221 --> 00:00:50.833
[eerie music continues]

16
00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.749
[Soldier] Hey. who are you?
You're not supposed to be here.

17
00:00:53.872 --> 00:00:56.484
[referee whistle blows]
Do you hear that?

18
00:00:57.511 --> 00:00:59.103
Maybe we should get in there.

19
00:00:59.128 --> 00:01:04.200
No... Sarge told us to hang
these up all around. come on.

20
00:01:04.475 --> 00:01:05.476
Lead the way.

21
00:01:05.658 --> 00:01:08.312
You lead the way.
Always tellin' me what to do.

22
00:01:09.547 --> 00:01:12.550
[gunshots]
[people shouting]

23
00:01:12.637 --> 00:01:14.770
[tense music]
[wind whipping]

24
00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:19.775
[tense music continues]
[shouting]

25
00:01:26.521 --> 00:01:30.090
[walkers growling]

26
00:01:44.713 --> 00:01:49.457
[gentle music]
[shovel thudding]

27
00:02:05.212 --> 00:02:08.128
[gentle music]

28
00:02:10.086 --> 00:02:11.653
What the hell are you doing?

29
00:02:15.004 --> 00:02:16.136
You were sleeping.

30
00:02:16.788 --> 00:02:18.549
-[Negan scoffing]
-Armstrong and I got to talking.

31
00:02:18.573 --> 00:02:21.880
She was <i>my</i> responsibility.
<i>Mine</i>!

32
00:02:22.403 --> 00:02:25.928
I was...
I was tryin' to do you a favor.

33
00:02:26.015 --> 00:02:27.415
You're still
healing from the wound.

34
00:02:27.451 --> 00:02:29.453
Where you stabbed me
in the goddamn back?

35
00:02:30.498 --> 00:02:31.658
Never ends with you. does it?

36
00:02:32.935 --> 00:02:35.416
Uh. first. you lure me
to this goddamn island.

37
00:02:35.503 --> 00:02:36.721
and then you lie to me.

38
00:02:37.505 --> 00:02:39.724
and then you hand me over
to some psychopath

39
00:02:39.855 --> 00:02:41.528
because you think you're
gonna get your son back.

40
00:02:41.552 --> 00:02:44.729
But you don't get your son back
because he sees the psychopath

41
00:02:44.816 --> 00:02:46.340
as the mama you'll never be.

42
00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:47.471
<i>Don't.</i>

43
00:02:47.906 --> 00:02:49.188
[Negan] Doesn't end there.
though. does it?

44
00:02:49.212 --> 00:02:50.561
No.

45
00:02:50.692 --> 00:02:53.085
Why don't you try murdering me
as the cherry on top

46
00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:55.566
of your shit sundae
of shit ideas

47
00:02:55.653 --> 00:02:57.829
and pretend you don't torch
everything you touch

48
00:02:58.265 --> 00:02:59.614
by burying the one person

49
00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:01.287
-on this godforsaken island...
-Listen to me!

50
00:03:01.311 --> 00:03:02.312
I am sorry.

51
00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:07.926
I'm sorry for what I did.
I'm sorry for what you lost.

52
00:03:09.014 --> 00:03:11.321
If I could undo anything
that's been done. I would.

53
00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:13.670
Would you?

54
00:03:15.107 --> 00:03:17.109
This... This is where we are.

55
00:03:17.936 --> 00:03:19.938
And we can either keep rehashing
all this shit

56
00:03:20.025 --> 00:03:21.865
that we can't change.
or we can try to move on.

57
00:03:23.246 --> 00:03:25.901
I have nothin' to move on to
thanks to you.

58
00:03:26.031 --> 00:03:29.600
[somber music]

59
00:03:29.687 --> 00:03:31.341
I'm stayin' put for Hershel.

60
00:03:34.083 --> 00:03:35.824
You got nothin'
and no one to stay put for.

61
00:03:35.911 --> 00:03:38.000
So why don't you go?
I'll help you pack your bags.

62
00:03:41.525 --> 00:03:42.525
Who are you kiddin'?

63
00:03:44.659 --> 00:03:45.834
You're never gonna let me go.

64
00:03:47.662 --> 00:03:50.186
All I am to you.
all I ever will be...

65
00:03:51.622 --> 00:03:54.364
is a big old shit pile
of the shittiest shit

66
00:03:54.495 --> 00:03:55.757
that I have ever done.

67
00:03:56.845 --> 00:03:57.933
The fact of the matter is.

68
00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:00.501
you need someone as shitty as me

69
00:04:00.588 --> 00:04:02.546
because I am
the only person shitty enough

70
00:04:02.633 --> 00:04:06.376
to make you feel less shitty
about your shit pile of a life.

71
00:04:06.507 --> 00:04:08.827
So do me a favor and go ahead
and keep twistin' that knife.

72
00:04:08.857 --> 00:04:11.816
because we both know
that is the one goddamn thing

73
00:04:11.947 --> 00:04:13.307
that you'll do
without screwin' up.

74
00:04:14.341 --> 00:04:18.780
Okay. then you fucking stab me.
Take it. Clean slate. Let's go.

75
00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:21.522
-[Maggie] Here.
-[chuckling]

76
00:04:22.436 --> 00:04:23.828
I don't wanna die. okay?

77
00:04:23.915 --> 00:04:25.937
But I will gladly bleed a little
if it'll make you shut

78
00:04:25.961 --> 00:04:27.441
that gapin' bullshit hole.

79
00:04:27.571 --> 00:04:30.618
So either do it or for the love
of God. <i>shut the fuck up.</i>

80
00:04:32.446 --> 00:04:33.360
It is a one-time offer

81
00:04:33.447 --> 00:04:34.883
with a ten-second
expiration date.

82
00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:37.277
so you better get to it... Ten.

83
00:04:37.625 --> 00:04:40.367
-Nine. eight. seven. six...
-You are batshit.

84
00:04:41.019 --> 00:04:43.587
Probably... Five. four...

85
00:04:43.935 --> 00:04:45.197
-Three...
-I'm gonna do it.

86
00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:48.549
-Do it! Two. one...
-[Renata] Drop your weapons!

87
00:04:48.636 --> 00:04:52.640
[dramatic music]

88
00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.294
She said drop your weapons!

89
00:04:55.991 --> 00:04:58.950
-You got bullets in those guns?
-You wanna find out?

90
00:05:02.084 --> 00:05:03.303
And whatever the hell that is.

91
00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.786
What is this. all right?
What do you want?

92
00:05:10.527 --> 00:05:12.355
We were on our way
to the cathedral

93
00:05:12.486 --> 00:05:13.617
to steal a methane tank.

94
00:05:14.357 --> 00:05:15.357
Heard you call him Negan.

95
00:05:17.665 --> 00:05:21.451
Rumor has it that's the name
of the Croat's #2.

96
00:05:23.018 --> 00:05:24.498
[Luis]
With your boy here as leverage?

97
00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:26.925
Our plan just got a hell
of a lot easier.

98
00:05:27.196 --> 00:05:28.196
My boy?

99
00:05:29.241 --> 00:05:30.330
He just had a knife on me.

100
00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:32.027
I've got nothin'
to do with this.

101
00:05:32.157 --> 00:05:33.333
Oh. she's lyin'.

102
00:05:33.463 --> 00:05:35.204
She is definitely the Croat's
#3.

103
00:05:35.291 --> 00:05:36.118
Listen to me. You...

104
00:05:36.248 --> 00:05:37.248
Both of you. shut up!

105
00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:38.749
-[Negan chuckling]
-[Renata] Go!

106
00:05:38.773 --> 00:05:39.773
You are makin' a mistake.

107
00:05:41.079 --> 00:05:42.080
The Croat is in the wind.

108
00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:43.517
It's New Babylon who's got
control

109
00:05:43.604 --> 00:05:45.083
of those methane tanks now.

110
00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:47.651
So if you want us to get close.
any of us. we get hanged:

111
00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:50.045
you. us. all of us.

112
00:05:52.439 --> 00:05:54.832
Bullshit. Get walking

113
00:05:55.877 --> 00:05:57.705
-Go.
-Come on. Come on.

114
00:05:57.835 --> 00:06:03.101
[tense music]

115
00:06:03.232 --> 00:06:04.992
-[Luis] <i>Alley on your right.</i>
-[Renata] <i>Clear.</i>

116
00:06:05.016 --> 00:06:08.629
[tense music continues]

117
00:06:08.716 --> 00:06:10.544
Is he your brother?
I see the resemblance.

118
00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:16.376
Yeah. He yours?

119
00:06:17.768 --> 00:06:20.031
No. Definitely no.

120
00:06:20.945 --> 00:06:22.512
Well. you sure
as hell fight like it.

121
00:06:23.644 --> 00:06:24.884
[Luis]
Cellar door on your left.

122
00:06:25.559 --> 00:06:26.559
[Renata] Looks clear.

123
00:06:26.951 --> 00:06:29.563
[Hershel] Mom? Mom?!

124
00:06:30.085 --> 00:06:32.217
-Hershel?
-Mom!

125
00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:37.614
[explosions rumbling]

126
00:06:37.745 --> 00:06:43.838
[dramatic music]

127
00:07:26.576 --> 00:07:28.317
[explosions rumbling]
[fire crackling]

128
00:07:29.884 --> 00:07:32.843
[shouting. screaming]

129
00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:38.936
[tense music]
[walkers groaning]

130
00:07:47.031 --> 00:07:51.122
-[Luis and Renata grunting]
-[walkers groaning]

131
00:07:51.209 --> 00:07:52.839
[Renata] All the dead
in this city are going

132
00:07:52.863 --> 00:07:54.952
to be coming this way
after that explosion.

133
00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:56.301
We need to find cover.

134
00:07:57.477 --> 00:07:58.565
We need to find Negan.

135
00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:05.049
[walker snarling]
[thudding]

136
00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:12.100
-[Negan grunting]
-[walker groaning and snarling]

137
00:08:13.405 --> 00:08:19.368
-[Negan grunting]
-[walkers groaning and snarling]

138
00:08:24.329 --> 00:08:27.768
[Maggie] Hershel!
Hershel. where are you?

139
00:08:28.551 --> 00:08:30.151
-Hershel. down here!
-[Hershel panting]

140
00:08:30.901 --> 00:08:31.922
[Maggie] Hershel!
Can you hear me?!

141
00:08:31.946 --> 00:08:33.382
Mom?

142
00:08:33.513 --> 00:08:37.517
-[Hershel coughing]
-[walkers growling]

143
00:08:39.431 --> 00:08:40.476
Hershel!

144
00:08:41.042 --> 00:08:44.132
[walker snarling]

145
00:08:46.308 --> 00:08:49.703
-[grunting]
-[walker growling]

146
00:08:51.835 --> 00:08:53.358
I'm sorry for this.

147
00:08:53.445 --> 00:08:56.840
-[Negan] For what?
-[Maggie grunting]

148
00:08:56.927 --> 00:08:59.582
-[Negan groaning]
-[Maggie] That.

149
00:09:00.322 --> 00:09:02.585
God. I so should've stabbed you.

150
00:09:02.672 --> 00:09:08.678
[dramatic music]
[walkers snarling]

151
00:09:25.521 --> 00:09:30.657
-[Negan groaning]
-[walkers growling and snarling]

152
00:09:30.787 --> 00:09:36.750
-[The Croat panting]
-[walkers growling and snarling]

153
00:09:40.797 --> 00:09:42.930
[grunting]

154
00:09:45.802 --> 00:09:49.763
Luis! [sighs] Luis.
you look terrible. my friend.

155
00:09:51.416 --> 00:09:52.853
You're gonna lead us
to the tanks.

156
00:09:54.028 --> 00:09:57.727
You're gonna give us one.
and then you're going to die.

157
00:09:59.294 --> 00:10:02.950
[walkers snarling]

158
00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:04.778
[grunts]

159
00:10:07.258 --> 00:10:08.258
The tanks?

160
00:10:08.956 --> 00:10:10.740
What do you think that explosion
was?

161
00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:13.438
Tanks are gone.

162
00:10:14.614 --> 00:10:17.617
-What?
-[The Croat] What I created?

163
00:10:18.705 --> 00:10:22.404
Falling into the hands of
those... New Babylon Visigoths?

164
00:10:23.405 --> 00:10:26.800
No. They had to be exploded.

165
00:10:27.931 --> 00:10:29.150
Then you'll make us one.

166
00:10:31.761 --> 00:10:33.589
There won't be
time enough for that.

167
00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:36.897
[dramatic music continues]
[The Croat breathes heavily]

168
00:10:38.202 --> 00:10:42.467
-[Negan groaning]
-[walkers snarling]

169
00:10:42.598 --> 00:10:48.604
[dramatic music continues]
[The Croat breathing heavily]

170
00:10:50.519 --> 00:10:54.392
No. Luis! No. no.
[speaks Spanish] Come on.

171
00:10:54.479 --> 00:10:56.656
It's not worth it. Luis...

172
00:10:56.743 --> 00:10:59.223
[dramatic music continues]

173
00:10:59.354 --> 00:11:01.965
-[Negan groaning]
-[walkers snarling]

174
00:11:02.096 --> 00:11:05.055
[rattling and thudding]

175
00:11:05.142 --> 00:11:11.148
-[Negan groaning and panting]
-[walker snarling]

176
00:11:14.282 --> 00:11:15.849
[sighs wearily]

177
00:11:20.592 --> 00:11:26.642
-[walker snarling]
-[Maggie grunting]

178
00:11:33.649 --> 00:11:34.844
[thudding. splat]
[walker grunts]

179
00:11:34.868 --> 00:11:38.132
[dramatic music continues]

180
00:11:38.262 --> 00:11:42.658
[walker snarling]

181
00:11:42.789 --> 00:11:44.007
All right. dickhead.

182
00:11:45.313 --> 00:11:46.706
I guess you get the honor.

183
00:11:46.793 --> 00:11:52.799
[suspenseful music]
[walker snarling]

184
00:11:54.452 --> 00:11:57.673
-Mom!? Are you down here?
-Over here!

185
00:11:58.195 --> 00:12:01.111
-[walker snarling]
-[Maggie grunting]

186
00:12:01.198 --> 00:12:04.767
Hershel...
[tense music]

187
00:12:04.854 --> 00:12:06.774
-Where's your wrists?
-[Maggie panting] Oh God.

188
00:12:14.559 --> 00:12:18.172
[dramatic music]
[walkers snarling]

189
00:12:18.302 --> 00:12:20.740
Luis. it is not safe out here.
We need cover.

190
00:12:23.307 --> 00:12:26.702
There!
[dramatic music continues]

191
00:12:28.791 --> 00:12:32.099
[walkers growling]

192
00:12:37.365 --> 00:12:38.365
What are you doin'?

193
00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:41.150
Renata...

194
00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:44.285
Damn it. leave him!

195
00:12:44.372 --> 00:12:47.767
[dramatic music continues]

196
00:12:47.854 --> 00:12:49.029
Shit!

197
00:12:49.159 --> 00:12:52.554
[dramatic music continues]
[Renata coughing]

198
00:13:02.433 --> 00:13:06.133
[Negan grunting]
[dramatic music continues]

199
00:13:06.263 --> 00:13:08.526
Negan!

200
00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:13.488
I had a feeling our paths would
cross again before the end.

201
00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:14.750
You.

202
00:13:14.837 --> 00:13:17.971
[suspenseful music]

203
00:13:20.016 --> 00:13:22.279
No. no!
Stop. stop. stop. stop! Please.

204
00:13:22.802 --> 00:13:23.842
We weren't gonna hurt you.

205
00:13:24.325 --> 00:13:26.675
We were just tryin'
to keep a baby alive.

206
00:13:26.806 --> 00:13:32.812
[dramatic music]

207
00:13:36.685 --> 00:13:38.861
[upbeat Latin music]

208
00:13:38.948 --> 00:13:41.603
[cork popping]
[cheering]

209
00:13:41.733 --> 00:13:44.606
[upbeat Latin music continues]
[indistinct chattering]

210
00:13:51.004 --> 00:13:53.404
[Renata] Yvette. the kids wanna
show you the stuffy they made

211
00:13:53.484 --> 00:13:55.008
for the baby.

212
00:13:55.095 --> 00:13:56.333
[Yvette. beyond touched]
Aww. It better not make me cry.

213
00:13:56.357 --> 00:13:59.882
-Aw. see. Tio Chucho loves it.
-[giggling]

214
00:13:59.969 --> 00:14:01.569
As if the world
weren't fucked up enough.

215
00:14:01.623 --> 00:14:03.775
now there's gonna be a little
Chucho runnin' around here?

216
00:14:03.799 --> 00:14:04.799
Can't believe it. dude.

217
00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:06.670
I love you. bro.

218
00:14:08.848 --> 00:14:09.761
[Luis] I love you. man.

219
00:14:09.849 --> 00:14:13.853
[upbeat Latin music continues]

220
00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:15.550
[music stops]

221
00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:18.379
No. no. no. no.
Don't stop on my account.

222
00:14:19.162 --> 00:14:20.642
You have much to celebrate.

223
00:14:22.426 --> 00:14:28.302
My eyes and ears tell me
your family is expanding. yes?

224
00:14:30.130 --> 00:14:31.261
Yes.

225
00:14:32.045 --> 00:14:33.481
Yvette and Chucho
are having a baby.

226
00:14:34.134 --> 00:14:35.134
[The Croat] Well. then.

227
00:14:35.962 --> 00:14:38.878
I suppose congratulations
are in order.

228
00:14:40.662 --> 00:14:46.407
Flowers from the cemetery.
And the world begins anew. eh?

229
00:14:49.366 --> 00:14:51.455
[tense music]

230
00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:54.806
And yet. Renata...

231
00:14:55.329 --> 00:15:00.377
all this at the very time I have
an issue to address with you.

232
00:15:03.990 --> 00:15:06.079
We have an arrangement. yes?

233
00:15:08.559 --> 00:15:09.909
We protect you.

234
00:15:13.042 --> 00:15:15.740
With respect.
the deal was forced on us.

235
00:15:15.827 --> 00:15:17.612
We didn't need it.

236
00:15:17.699 --> 00:15:20.093
So why don't we just end it?

237
00:15:22.051 --> 00:15:23.923
The Burazi protect this island.

238
00:15:25.837 --> 00:15:27.757
The deal ends when you leave it.
Are you leaving?

239
00:15:29.493 --> 00:15:31.297
[Ramon] Our family's been here
a hell of a lot longer

240
00:15:31.321 --> 00:15:32.321
than you guys have.

241
00:15:36.065 --> 00:15:37.632
Well. good for you.

242
00:15:39.025 --> 00:15:40.461
But the arrangement stands.

243
00:15:43.072 --> 00:15:44.944
And the Dama's vision
of the future?

244
00:15:49.296 --> 00:15:52.952
Well. it only succeeds if
everyone contributes something

245
00:15:53.213 --> 00:15:55.606
valuable in return.

246
00:15:57.347 --> 00:16:02.309
And as much as I want to
believe you can... I don't.

247
00:16:05.355 --> 00:16:06.593
I was training some of
the others

248
00:16:06.617 --> 00:16:07.618
in emergency medicine.

249
00:16:09.142 --> 00:16:11.274
Okay... Doctors!

250
00:16:12.623 --> 00:16:15.583
Doctors are a resource!

251
00:16:18.499 --> 00:16:21.458
Your brother Chucho!
[laughs]

252
00:16:21.589 --> 00:16:23.504
Is he among your trainees?

253
00:16:26.463 --> 00:16:27.638
He is.

254
00:16:32.382 --> 00:16:33.514
Well. Doctor Chucho.

255
00:16:34.732 --> 00:16:35.995
let me take a look at you.

256
00:16:37.909 --> 00:16:38.910
Come. come. come.

257
00:16:39.476 --> 00:16:42.827
[tense music]
[The Croat] So...

258
00:16:45.787 --> 00:16:48.485
Are you a resource. Doctor?

259
00:16:49.356 --> 00:16:53.795
[tense music continues]

260
00:16:54.448 --> 00:16:55.623
Yes.

261
00:16:57.146 --> 00:16:58.365
Well. then prove it.

262
00:16:59.192 --> 00:17:02.673
[knife thudding]
[gasping. exclaiming]

263
00:17:03.544 --> 00:17:07.504
-No. no. no.
-[indistinct clamoring]

264
00:17:07.591 --> 00:17:09.637
I've given you a patient.
Doctor.

265
00:17:10.768 --> 00:17:11.769
Save him.

266
00:17:12.857 --> 00:17:14.257
Don't leave me. <i>tio</i>.
Don't leave me!

267
00:17:14.294 --> 00:17:16.470
-Stay with me. Stay with me.
-[Ramon groaning]

268
00:17:16.905 --> 00:17:20.430
You know... I fear he is not
too good at this.

269
00:17:20.517 --> 00:17:21.866
Maybe you are a bad teacher?

270
00:17:23.955 --> 00:17:27.394
Or maybe you are lying to me
about this whole business?

271
00:17:27.872 --> 00:17:31.050
[Chucho] Don't leave me. <i>tio</i>.
[speaking Spanish]

272
00:17:31.137 --> 00:17:33.748
Just look at me. <i>tio</i>. No!

273
00:17:37.099 --> 00:17:38.709
[The Croat] Huh...

274
00:17:43.888 --> 00:17:49.938
[panting]

275
00:17:52.941 --> 00:17:54.073
I have no choice.

276
00:17:57.902 --> 00:18:01.689
-You just don't make the cut.
-No!

277
00:18:01.819 --> 00:18:05.606
[group screaming. crying]

278
00:18:06.998 --> 00:18:08.261
[gurgles]

279
00:18:09.523 --> 00:18:12.352
[sobs hysterically]

280
00:18:15.398 --> 00:18:16.834
Yvette...
[speaks Spanish]

281
00:18:16.965 --> 00:18:20.577
You know.
<i>I</i> was someone's trainee once.

282
00:18:20.925 --> 00:18:22.362
Hopefully better than Chucho.

283
00:18:23.711 --> 00:18:27.018
And one of the many things
my mentor taught me was

284
00:18:27.106 --> 00:18:28.933
that killing the right person

285
00:18:29.456 --> 00:18:34.939
at the right time makes
everyone else fall in line.

286
00:18:36.419 --> 00:18:38.595
So. I wonder...

287
00:18:41.642 --> 00:18:46.125
Did I pick the right person...
persons?

288
00:18:48.649 --> 00:18:50.564
Maybe we should
try this again. huh?

289
00:18:52.609 --> 00:18:54.568
Who shall be the next patient. huh?

290
00:18:55.090 --> 00:18:56.265
Huh?

291
00:18:58.485 --> 00:19:02.706
Eenie. meenie. miney...

292
00:19:02.793 --> 00:19:07.233
Renata... Oh. Renata...

293
00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:08.843
Do you really believe one

294
00:19:08.973 --> 00:19:11.846
of those slapdash weapons
can save your family?

295
00:19:15.893 --> 00:19:18.200
Everybody back.
[speaks Spanish]

296
00:19:18.287 --> 00:19:24.206
[gas hissing]

297
00:19:24.467 --> 00:19:25.599
I'm willing to die for them.

298
00:19:27.253 --> 00:19:28.515
Are you?

299
00:19:30.691 --> 00:19:32.475
I don't think you would.

300
00:19:33.476 --> 00:19:34.869
You don't know me very well.

301
00:19:34.999 --> 00:19:41.049
[gas hissing]

302
00:19:45.271 --> 00:19:49.100
This isn't over. For any of you.

303
00:19:49.188 --> 00:19:51.494
[gas hissing]

304
00:19:51.625 --> 00:19:55.324
Again... Congratulations.

305
00:19:55.411 --> 00:20:01.374
[gas hissing]
[tense music]

306
00:20:05.856 --> 00:20:10.209
No. Chucho! No. Chucho!
Chucho. please?

307
00:20:10.296 --> 00:20:16.302
[sobbing]
[somber music]

308
00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:26.399
[walkers snarling]

309
00:20:28.662 --> 00:20:31.099
[Hershel] They're closed.
but there's no lock.

310
00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:32.468
My sister-in-law is
having her baby.

311
00:20:32.492 --> 00:20:33.797
We need to go now.

312
00:20:33.928 --> 00:20:35.732
All right. well.
walkers are swarming out there.

313
00:20:35.756 --> 00:20:37.386
There's nothing any of us can
do about that.

314
00:20:37.410 --> 00:20:40.848
[walkers groaning faintly]

315
00:20:41.370 --> 00:20:42.478
[Maggie] Nobody is going
anywhere.

316
00:20:42.502 --> 00:20:48.508
[walkers groaning faintly]

317
00:20:51.032 --> 00:20:52.966
He and I are gonna make sure
that this place is safe.

318
00:20:52.990 --> 00:20:54.270
If you would just let us
explain.

319
00:20:54.296 --> 00:20:55.534
The baby is coming
two months early...

320
00:20:55.558 --> 00:20:56.998
-Nobody...
-[Renata] If we don't...

321
00:20:57.908 --> 00:21:00.868
kill anybody until we get back.

322
00:21:01.172 --> 00:21:07.135
[dramatic music]
[walkers groaning faintly]

323
00:21:24.587 --> 00:21:26.459
There's another door
up the stairs.

324
00:21:26.546 --> 00:21:28.461
There may be a way out.
but it's secure.

325
00:21:29.288 --> 00:21:30.289
Okay.

326
00:21:32.421 --> 00:21:33.941
-How did you...
-I know Ginny's dead.

327
00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:37.165
You know?

328
00:21:38.427 --> 00:21:39.646
I saw you bury her.

329
00:21:42.953 --> 00:21:44.477
And I went looking for you.
and...

330
00:21:46.827 --> 00:21:48.747
Just wanted to see if
you were really gonna stay.

331
00:21:51.092 --> 00:21:52.212
You thought that I wouldn't?

332
00:21:54.051 --> 00:21:55.411
I wouldn't blame
you if you didn't.

333
00:21:59.405 --> 00:22:01.320
When I got back. the Dama...

334
00:22:03.017 --> 00:22:04.017
She knew what I did.

335
00:22:04.801 --> 00:22:06.881
She started talkin' about how it
wasn't enough for me

336
00:22:06.934 --> 00:22:08.414
to hurt you.

337
00:22:12.592 --> 00:22:13.593
She told me I had to...

338
00:22:16.465 --> 00:22:18.032
She told me I had to <i>kill</i> you.

339
00:22:20.339 --> 00:22:21.779
Just like how I told you
to kill <i>him</i>.

340
00:22:24.430 --> 00:22:26.040
I... I think it came from her.

341
00:22:27.868 --> 00:22:29.696
Just being around her.

342
00:22:32.394 --> 00:22:34.962
And I just didn't see it.
And I should've.

343
00:22:35.397 --> 00:22:38.095
[Maggie]
No. It's what she does. Hershel.

344
00:22:38.705 --> 00:22:41.838
She sees what people
are looking for. what they need.

345
00:22:42.186 --> 00:22:44.363
and she uses it
to get what she wants.

346
00:22:46.452 --> 00:22:48.412
It's easier than you would
think to lose yourself.

347
00:22:51.021 --> 00:22:55.069
And you were right to be mad.
Because I wasn't there.

348
00:22:58.638 --> 00:23:00.379
Yeah. after she told me to...

349
00:23:02.859 --> 00:23:04.819
I started thinkin' about
the times you <i>were</i> there.

350
00:23:07.211 --> 00:23:09.083
the scary things
you made go away.

351
00:23:12.826 --> 00:23:14.088
You made it so I had a life.

352
00:23:17.178 --> 00:23:22.270
I don't want to spend it being
mad anymore. at you. at anyone.

353
00:23:24.315 --> 00:23:25.621
Me neither.

354
00:23:25.708 --> 00:23:31.758
[gentle music]

355
00:23:40.723 --> 00:23:42.323
[Maggie] She's not gonna hurt us
anymore.

356
00:23:43.073 --> 00:23:46.773
I won't let her.
We won't let her.

357
00:23:48.296 --> 00:23:50.298
Soon as it's safe.
we're gonna get out of here.

358
00:23:51.038 --> 00:23:53.954
go home. and start over.

359
00:23:57.958 --> 00:24:00.221
Hershel.
you're gonna move mountains.

360
00:24:01.440 --> 00:24:04.355
[angry shouting]

361
00:24:04.660 --> 00:24:06.053
[yelling in Spanish]

362
00:24:06.183 --> 00:24:07.552
[The Croat] You said Yvette is
only 7 months pregnant!

363
00:24:07.576 --> 00:24:11.014
Luis. how can I help you
with your hand on my throat?

364
00:24:11.188 --> 00:24:14.627
-[Maggie] Hey. hey!
-[angry shouting]

365
00:24:16.977 --> 00:24:19.153
Were you gonna do anything
to try to stop this?

366
00:24:19.762 --> 00:24:21.722
No. I'm puttin' the little ball
in the little cup.

367
00:24:22.809 --> 00:24:24.288
[The Croat breathing heavily]

368
00:24:24.419 --> 00:24:26.266
[Luis] This sociopath killed our
brother right in front of us

369
00:24:26.290 --> 00:24:27.814
and our uncle.

370
00:24:27.944 --> 00:24:31.644
[The Croat] Okay. maybe...
Maybe I handled things badly.

371
00:24:33.559 --> 00:24:35.996
But I was just trying
to make a point.

372
00:24:36.431 --> 00:24:38.825
-As my mentor taught me.
-[Renata] Mentor?

373
00:24:48.399 --> 00:24:50.837
You said you would help.

374
00:24:55.885 --> 00:25:01.587
They know the baby needs
an incubator to have any chance.

375
00:25:01.674 --> 00:25:02.849
And a tank would make it run.

376
00:25:03.589 --> 00:25:05.242
You need to show us how
to build one now.

377
00:25:05.765 --> 00:25:06.765
There's no need to build.

378
00:25:08.507 --> 00:25:09.595
There's still a tank left.

379
00:25:11.814 --> 00:25:17.211
There is a single prototype
I hid away a long time ago

380
00:25:19.822 --> 00:25:23.217
with plans and detail how
to make more.

381
00:25:23.739 --> 00:25:25.175
Where? Where is it?

382
00:25:26.002 --> 00:25:28.788
Oh and I tell you and he kills
me? No.

383
00:25:30.703 --> 00:25:32.879
My story does not end
in a musty basement.

384
00:25:34.097 --> 00:25:38.058
No. I'll show you.
It's not far from here.

385
00:25:38.885 --> 00:25:39.885
So we go now.

386
00:25:41.061 --> 00:25:42.410
He shows us where the tank is.

387
00:25:42.715 --> 00:25:45.128
Our family's still waiting at
the hospital with the generator.

388
00:25:45.152 --> 00:25:48.111
I told you. you're not gonna
last five minutes out there.

389
00:25:48.242 --> 00:25:49.785
We don't know how long
he'll last <i>in here</i>.

390
00:25:49.809 --> 00:25:51.114
Luis. she's right.

391
00:25:51.550 --> 00:25:53.377
We are no good to anyone dead. okay?

392
00:25:53.464 --> 00:25:55.728
We wait it out here as long
as we can and <i>then</i> we go.

393
00:25:55.815 --> 00:25:59.383
Listen to her. Luis.
Because what I'm offering

394
00:26:00.341 --> 00:26:02.561
has value far beyond
the child's life.

395
00:26:03.518 --> 00:26:04.518
It's my legacy.

396
00:26:06.390 --> 00:26:09.655
Imagine your homes
with steady power.

397
00:26:10.481 --> 00:26:13.746
your own fields to plow.
fauna to hunt.

398
00:26:14.921 --> 00:26:16.575
all surrounded by water.

399
00:26:21.057 --> 00:26:22.057
This island...

400
00:26:24.365 --> 00:26:25.845
It could be your fortress...

401
00:26:27.760 --> 00:26:28.760
Forever.

402
00:26:32.199 --> 00:26:33.592
We just wanna save this baby.

403
00:26:35.419 --> 00:26:38.466
And we will. [speaks Spanish]

404
00:26:40.207 --> 00:26:41.207
When it's safe.

405
00:26:42.862 --> 00:26:45.299
we could use some good fighters
to help us out there.

406
00:26:45.429 --> 00:26:47.867
[gentle music]
[cup popping]

407
00:26:52.567 --> 00:26:53.960
You can save this baby.

408
00:26:54.700 --> 00:26:57.485
Haven't you learned by now what
happens to people stupid enough

409
00:26:57.572 --> 00:26:59.139
to have hope in this world?

410
00:27:01.532 --> 00:27:03.317
Look. I'm sorry.

411
00:27:04.623 --> 00:27:06.320
You can try whatever
you want here.

412
00:27:06.450 --> 00:27:09.497
but that baby
doesn't have a chance.

413
00:27:12.108 --> 00:27:13.153
Oh. wow.

414
00:27:15.155 --> 00:27:16.243
You're a real fighter.

415
00:27:19.072 --> 00:27:20.247
[cup and ball clank]

416
00:27:20.769 --> 00:27:21.683
You're right.

417
00:27:21.770 --> 00:27:27.820
[tense music]

418
00:27:35.392 --> 00:27:36.655
Where are you goin'?

419
00:27:38.178 --> 00:27:39.178
We're in a bar. right?

420
00:27:40.746 --> 00:27:41.786
I'm gonna go find a drink.

421
00:27:42.182 --> 00:27:45.925
[walkers growling faintly]

422
00:27:47.230 --> 00:27:51.104
[unsettling music]
[walkers growling]

423
00:27:59.242 --> 00:28:03.682
[walker snarling]

424
00:28:15.302 --> 00:28:21.308
-[walker snarling]
-[Dillard whistling]

425
00:28:28.924 --> 00:28:30.075
[Dillard]
She's still being that way?

426
00:28:30.099 --> 00:28:31.884
[walker snarling]

427
00:28:32.188 --> 00:28:34.016
[Dillard] And what'd ya say to
her?

428
00:28:34.625 --> 00:28:37.105
[Dillard] Well. have you thought
about... [groans like walker]?

429
00:28:37.585 --> 00:28:40.719
That's classic Titicaca.
Don't you wish that... okay.

430
00:28:40.849 --> 00:28:42.068
[laughs]
I hear you. buddy.

431
00:28:42.198 --> 00:28:43.243
[floor creaking]

432
00:28:54.297 --> 00:28:55.297
Hey there. <i>amigo.</i>

433
00:29:00.173 --> 00:29:01.759
Quite the fustercluck out there. amiright?

434
00:29:01.783 --> 00:29:03.437
[chuckling]

435
00:29:05.482 --> 00:29:06.745
You wanna pull up a stool?

436
00:29:07.833 --> 00:29:09.008
Me and Cockenspiel's

437
00:29:09.138 --> 00:29:10.818
about to start a game
of Fuck. Marry. Kill.

438
00:29:10.923 --> 00:29:12.315
And Titicaca's bein'
a wet blanket.

439
00:29:12.402 --> 00:29:14.709
so we could use a third.

440
00:29:16.972 --> 00:29:19.453
And don't worry.
I made these guys nice and safe.

441
00:29:21.063 --> 00:29:24.197
Name's Dillard. Skunky brewski?

442
00:29:27.417 --> 00:29:28.417
Sure.

443
00:29:30.725 --> 00:29:32.268
[Dillard] I thought pullin'
teeth would be hard.

444
00:29:32.292 --> 00:29:34.294
but those nails were
a real son of a bitch.

445
00:29:34.424 --> 00:29:36.949
-[walker growling]
-[Negan chuckling]

446
00:29:37.993 --> 00:29:39.603
[Dillard] He likes you.
[chuckles]

447
00:29:39.690 --> 00:29:40.735
Thank you.

448
00:29:40.822 --> 00:29:43.303
Welcome to the bar.

449
00:29:44.173 --> 00:29:45.218
[glass ringing]
Cheers.

450
00:29:45.348 --> 00:29:46.348
[Dillard chuckling]

451
00:29:49.744 --> 00:29:55.663
[walkers snarling]

452
00:30:00.276 --> 00:30:01.800
Okay. That should hold.

453
00:30:06.456 --> 00:30:08.328
You could've left
the Croat to die.

454
00:30:09.024 --> 00:30:10.025
You didn't.

455
00:30:11.026 --> 00:30:12.946
And because of you.
that baby still has a chance.

456
00:30:14.334 --> 00:30:16.815
[walkers snarling faintly]

457
00:30:20.993 --> 00:30:24.953
San Lazaro.
patron saint of hope and mercy.

458
00:30:26.433 --> 00:30:27.433
It belonged to my dad.

459
00:30:29.958 --> 00:30:32.047
He always told us
that we had a choice.

460
00:30:32.918 --> 00:30:37.357
We could choose the fight
or we could choose the light.

461
00:30:38.575 --> 00:30:44.016
[thudding]
[walkers snarling faintly]

462
00:30:48.585 --> 00:30:51.458
[Hershel] So you can just
forgive the Croat

463
00:30:51.545 --> 00:30:53.242
-after what he did?
-[Renata] No.

464
00:30:53.329 --> 00:30:56.245
Never. Making him suffer...

465
00:30:56.332 --> 00:30:57.657
I think about
that every single day.

466
00:30:57.681 --> 00:31:03.905
[gentle music]

467
00:31:03.992 --> 00:31:07.474
But once the killing starts.
when does it stop?

468
00:31:07.604 --> 00:31:13.697
[gentle music continues]

469
00:31:16.657 --> 00:31:19.747
You know. choosing
the light after that...

470
00:31:21.575 --> 00:31:23.015
was the hardest
thing I've ever done.

471
00:31:25.013 --> 00:31:26.101
It still is.

472
00:31:26.232 --> 00:31:31.193
[gentle music continues]

473
00:31:31.280 --> 00:31:33.413
But it's a choice
that I wanna keep making.

474
00:31:35.067 --> 00:31:36.416
Me. too.

475
00:31:40.724 --> 00:31:42.030
Just started.

476
00:31:44.859 --> 00:31:47.775
Maybe when we're done here.

477
00:31:47.906 --> 00:31:50.604
Luis can take a look
at Negan's back.

478
00:31:51.039 --> 00:31:53.781
I put a knife
into it last night.

479
00:31:55.348 --> 00:31:56.348
[Renata] Oh.

480
00:31:56.827 --> 00:32:00.222
You. like. just just started.

481
00:32:00.353 --> 00:32:03.965
[walkers snarling faintly]

482
00:32:04.487 --> 00:32:07.621
[walker snarling]

483
00:32:07.751 --> 00:32:08.927
Okay.

484
00:32:10.058 --> 00:32:13.061
[snarling continues]

485
00:32:14.323 --> 00:32:15.759
That is dastardly!

486
00:32:15.846 --> 00:32:17.631
Fuck. that is fresh.
Cockenspiel.

487
00:32:17.718 --> 00:32:19.024
[Negan chuckles]

488
00:32:19.154 --> 00:32:21.243
He's gonna kill Audrey Hep.
marry Venus Williams.

489
00:32:21.722 --> 00:32:24.159
And he says he's gonna bang
Barbara Bush like a screen door

490
00:32:24.246 --> 00:32:25.246
in a twister.

491
00:32:26.901 --> 00:32:28.120
I gotta ask.

492
00:32:29.904 --> 00:32:30.949
Where are you from. man?

493
00:32:31.079 --> 00:32:33.342
What planet do you come from?

494
00:32:33.864 --> 00:32:35.954
Well. I'm actually from Earth.
I'm from here.

495
00:32:37.346 --> 00:32:39.305
Upstairs studio apartment
actually.

496
00:32:39.435 --> 00:32:41.307
from way before shit
went tits up.

497
00:32:42.917 --> 00:32:47.487
So you have survived here
alone this whole time?

498
00:32:48.357 --> 00:32:49.357
How?

499
00:32:50.490 --> 00:32:51.510
[Dillard] So. over the years.

500
00:32:51.534 --> 00:32:53.319
folks either cut bait or
croaked.

501
00:32:54.059 --> 00:32:55.059
But I stayed.

502
00:32:55.712 --> 00:32:59.368
And I stayed above dirt by
turnin' each floor into a link

503
00:32:59.499 --> 00:33:00.500
in a CLVFC.

504
00:33:02.284 --> 00:33:04.678
Closed Loop Vertical Food Chain. okay?

505
00:33:05.070 --> 00:33:06.395
It starts with the deadies
who go slipin'

506
00:33:06.419 --> 00:33:07.579
'n slidin' into the basement.

507
00:33:10.684 --> 00:33:12.773
Here we got those maggoes
maggin' on the deadie...

508
00:33:12.903 --> 00:33:18.866
[upbeat music]
[flies buzzing]

509
00:33:22.087 --> 00:33:24.108
Then you got the froggies
froggin' on the maggoes...

510
00:33:24.132 --> 00:33:28.267
[upbeat music continues]
[frogs croaking]

511
00:33:28.354 --> 00:33:30.434
Of course we got the turks
turkin' on the froggies...

512
00:33:32.053 --> 00:33:33.493
Chain goes all
the way up to coyotes.

513
00:33:33.707 --> 00:33:35.347
which are surprisingly delish.
by the way.

514
00:33:35.578 --> 00:33:37.667
But I am happy to pump
the brakes on turkeys

515
00:33:38.103 --> 00:33:39.383
if you're feelin' kinda peckish.

516
00:33:40.453 --> 00:33:44.674
[lock rattling]

517
00:33:46.807 --> 00:33:48.678
Did baloney used to be illegal?

518
00:33:53.509 --> 00:33:55.381
[lock rattling]

519
00:33:58.732 --> 00:34:01.213
Infection is spreading faster
than I'd hoped.

520
00:34:02.910 --> 00:34:03.910
How can you tell?

521
00:34:05.217 --> 00:34:06.348
Rising body temperature.

522
00:34:07.393 --> 00:34:09.371
redness and swelling growing
outward from the wound.

523
00:34:09.395 --> 00:34:11.571
And see this pus
and milky drainage right there?

524
00:34:12.441 --> 00:34:13.441
Not good.

525
00:34:14.791 --> 00:34:15.791
What can I do to help?

526
00:34:17.881 --> 00:34:19.709
Use that water
to clean the wound.

527
00:34:20.319 --> 00:34:21.759
I'll find something
to dress it with.

528
00:34:24.410 --> 00:34:25.889
[Renata] So you think

529
00:34:26.020 --> 00:34:28.340
with those plans you could bring
electricity to the Bricks?

530
00:34:28.718 --> 00:34:31.417
We got someone there who used
to be a plumber tryin'

531
00:34:31.504 --> 00:34:32.504
to figure it out.

532
00:34:33.680 --> 00:34:35.421
My cousin Solmari's an engineer.

533
00:34:43.168 --> 00:34:44.560
You should come back with us.

534
00:34:46.171 --> 00:34:48.912
I mean. it's... It has been
hard there with the crops.

535
00:34:48.999 --> 00:34:51.741
Really hard... But with power...

536
00:34:53.961 --> 00:34:55.521
it could be a fresh start
for all of us.

537
00:34:58.705 --> 00:34:59.836
And I need a fresh start.

538
00:34:59.923 --> 00:35:05.973
[tense music]

539
00:35:07.931 --> 00:35:09.281
So what kinda doctor are you?

540
00:35:11.500 --> 00:35:13.111
Emergency medicine.

541
00:35:14.460 --> 00:35:16.340
I'd been training my brother
before the Croat...

542
00:35:17.593 --> 00:35:22.946
[somber music]

543
00:35:23.033 --> 00:35:24.774
Had to brain my uncle after.

544
00:35:26.994 --> 00:35:31.781
But when it came to Chucho.
I just... I couldn't.

545
00:35:35.742 --> 00:35:37.047
You and your people.

546
00:35:37.135 --> 00:35:39.267
you could come with me
and Hershel to The Bricks.

547
00:35:41.791 --> 00:35:42.791
Thanks.

548
00:35:43.706 --> 00:35:49.016
But this godforsaken city has
been our home for generations.

549
00:35:53.194 --> 00:35:54.194
The Croat's right.

550
00:35:55.370 --> 00:35:56.850
The city could
still be our home.

551
00:35:56.937 --> 00:36:00.680
[gentle music]

552
00:36:00.767 --> 00:36:02.986
[The Croat coughing]

553
00:36:05.337 --> 00:36:07.295
[Luis] Hey. where's the tank?

554
00:36:09.906 --> 00:36:11.169
Tell us where it is.

555
00:36:12.474 --> 00:36:14.041
No. I'm coming with you.

556
00:36:15.085 --> 00:36:16.348
End where I began.

557
00:36:19.089 --> 00:36:20.221
It's not far...

558
00:36:20.700 --> 00:36:22.060
[Luis]
He doesn't have much longer.

559
00:36:23.050 --> 00:36:24.182
We need to go now.

560
00:36:25.574 --> 00:36:27.707
[The Croat coughing]

561
00:36:30.231 --> 00:36:33.321
I know it's not safe out there.
but we need your help.

562
00:36:35.323 --> 00:36:38.370
We should help. At least try.

563
00:36:42.374 --> 00:36:43.201
Okay.

564
00:36:43.288 --> 00:36:49.337
[dramatic music]

565
00:36:53.080 --> 00:36:57.519
[walkers snarling]

566
00:37:03.308 --> 00:37:05.388
[Dillard] And if I had
spilled the beans on that one.

567
00:37:05.571 --> 00:37:08.617
let's just say a whole boatload
of people would've had diarrhea.

568
00:37:08.878 --> 00:37:10.793
-That is not appetizing.
-It's not.

569
00:37:10.880 --> 00:37:12.404
Oh. shit.

570
00:37:16.364 --> 00:37:18.584
Hello. Mason W. Dillard.

571
00:37:20.977 --> 00:37:22.109
Welcome.

572
00:37:24.285 --> 00:37:26.200
The Croat.
he doesn't have much time.

573
00:37:26.287 --> 00:37:28.420
We have to go now.

574
00:37:29.464 --> 00:37:30.987
What's the point?

575
00:37:31.727 --> 00:37:33.947
I know that you think that
baby's dead. but that mother.

576
00:37:34.034 --> 00:37:35.949
I know what she's been through.

577
00:37:36.036 --> 00:37:37.951
I know what she's
going through right now.

578
00:37:40.258 --> 00:37:43.348
We need numbers.
Please. We need you.

579
00:37:43.739 --> 00:37:44.977
All right. well.
you need numbers.

580
00:37:45.001 --> 00:37:46.873
why don't you ask my pal here.
Dillard?

581
00:37:47.395 --> 00:37:48.570
I ain't goin' nowhere.

582
00:37:55.142 --> 00:37:56.142
I need <i>you.</i>

583
00:37:56.448 --> 00:38:00.452
[gentle music]

584
00:38:01.975 --> 00:38:03.542
I finally got my son back.

585
00:38:04.020 --> 00:38:06.196
and I need to know that
I'm not gonna lose him again.

586
00:38:06.327 --> 00:38:08.416
I need to know
that things can work out.

587
00:38:08.895 --> 00:38:10.157
They can't. Maggie.

588
00:38:11.637 --> 00:38:14.944
Without you.
you're probably right.

589
00:38:17.904 --> 00:38:19.035
I'm tired of bein' angry.

590
00:38:19.427 --> 00:38:22.517
[gentle music continues]

591
00:38:22.604 --> 00:38:23.604
Aren't you?

592
00:38:24.476 --> 00:38:26.129
[gentle music continues]

593
00:38:27.174 --> 00:38:28.784
After it's done.
Luis can stitch you up

594
00:38:28.915 --> 00:38:31.961
and you can be free of me.
free to do whatever you want.

595
00:38:32.048 --> 00:38:35.835
I just... I need this
one last thing from you.

596
00:38:39.969 --> 00:38:41.319
Please.

597
00:38:43.059 --> 00:38:47.455
[gentle music continues]

598
00:38:58.640 --> 00:38:59.640
God damn it.

599
00:39:00.642 --> 00:39:02.644
I was just gettin'
all comfy and settled.

600
00:39:02.949 --> 00:39:04.385
I <i>really</i> should've stabbed you.

601
00:39:04.690 --> 00:39:05.865
You weren't gonna stab me.

602
00:39:05.952 --> 00:39:08.346
Oh. I was <i>so</i> gonna stab
you a little bit.

603
00:39:11.958 --> 00:39:17.877
[tense music]
[walkers growling]

604
00:39:19.008 --> 00:39:21.881
-How much further?
-We're close.

605
00:39:23.404 --> 00:39:25.493
-It's just ahead.
-Ahead where?

606
00:39:26.102 --> 00:39:27.843
[Renata] He needs to tell us
where to go!

607
00:39:27.974 --> 00:39:29.236
[Maggie] I got an idea.

608
00:39:29.367 --> 00:39:31.207
Your mother. she sacrificed
everything for you.

609
00:39:31.934 --> 00:39:34.067
-What would she say?
-[speaking Croatian]

610
00:39:34.850 --> 00:39:37.636
Her legacy. your legacy.
is about to disappear forever.

611
00:39:37.723 --> 00:39:40.203
-Come on.
-[speaking Croatian]

612
00:39:42.815 --> 00:39:43.935
Does anybody speak Croatian?

613
00:39:44.033 --> 00:39:46.688
[dramatic music]

614
00:39:46.775 --> 00:39:49.212
Wait. I think I know where it
is. Keep goin'.

615
00:39:49.299 --> 00:39:55.262
[dramatic music continues]
[walkers growling]

616
00:39:56.089 --> 00:39:58.308
[Renata grunting]

617
00:39:58.396 --> 00:40:00.572
[dramatic music continues]

618
00:40:08.362 --> 00:40:10.277
[Negan] Okay. we're almost
there.

619
00:40:16.152 --> 00:40:17.912
I think we're just gonna have
a seat. Maggie.

620
00:40:17.937 --> 00:40:23.943
[dramatic music continues]

621
00:40:30.732 --> 00:40:31.732
Okay.

622
00:40:31.777 --> 00:40:37.783
[dramatic music continues]

623
00:40:39.480 --> 00:40:40.786
Oh. sorry... I know.

624
00:40:40.916 --> 00:40:46.966
[somber music]

625
00:40:53.538 --> 00:40:56.802
I was so arrogant.

626
00:40:57.716 --> 00:40:59.326
I tried to lead...

627
00:41:03.548 --> 00:41:04.810
someone who only knows...

628
00:41:08.204 --> 00:41:09.031
How to lead.

629
00:41:09.118 --> 00:41:15.168
[somber music continues]

630
00:41:18.780 --> 00:41:20.173
Hey...

631
00:41:20.260 --> 00:41:25.700
[somber music continues]

632
00:41:25.787 --> 00:41:27.136
[speaking Croatian]

633
00:41:27.223 --> 00:41:33.186
[somber music continues]
[Negan crying]

634
00:41:38.017 --> 00:41:44.023
[flag rattling]
[somber music continues]

635
00:41:50.333 --> 00:41:53.859
[sniffling]
[somber music continues]

636
00:41:57.427 --> 00:42:02.389
[dramatic music]

637
00:42:03.695 --> 00:42:06.306
-Solmari. We got it.
-Oh. thank God!

638
00:42:06.436 --> 00:42:07.525
Through those doors.

639
00:42:07.655 --> 00:42:09.352
She's in the O.R.
Contractions are close.

640
00:42:09.439 --> 00:42:10.876
-Take this.
-Can I help?

641
00:42:11.616 --> 00:42:12.616
C'mon.

642
00:42:14.401 --> 00:42:15.881
-[Renata] Evie!
-[Yvette moans]

643
00:42:15.968 --> 00:42:17.404
Evie. we're here.

644
00:42:17.926 --> 00:42:20.189
<i>Mira.</i> Solmari is setting up
the tank across the hall.

645
00:42:20.276 --> 00:42:23.410
-[speaking Spanish]
-[laughing happily]

646
00:42:25.804 --> 00:42:26.924
The baby's head is crowning.

647
00:42:27.370 --> 00:42:29.851
Yvette. I'm gonna need you
to start pushing. okay?

648
00:42:30.460 --> 00:42:32.201
I need blankets. water to boil.

649
00:42:32.288 --> 00:42:33.848
and an extension cord for the
incubator.

650
00:42:33.942 --> 00:42:37.772
[Renata] Okay!
[speaks Spanish]

651
00:42:37.903 --> 00:42:43.909
[gentle music]

652
00:42:46.738 --> 00:42:47.608
Okay.

653
00:42:47.695 --> 00:42:50.393
[gentle music continues]

654
00:42:50.480 --> 00:42:52.787
Come on. That's a good push.

655
00:42:53.222 --> 00:42:55.050
-Another one just like that.
-Okay.

656
00:42:55.181 --> 00:42:57.662
Push <i>.</i> Good. good. good.

657
00:42:58.619 --> 00:43:02.449
-[Luis] C'mon.
-[gasping and panting]

658
00:43:03.885 --> 00:43:04.930
Solmari?

659
00:43:05.017 --> 00:43:06.148
When you're done over there.

660
00:43:06.235 --> 00:43:07.822
I need you to come here
and help Hershel.

661
00:43:07.846 --> 00:43:08.847
Why? Where are you going?

662
00:43:08.934 --> 00:43:10.892
[dramatic music]

663
00:43:10.979 --> 00:43:11.850
Tanks need methane.

664
00:43:11.937 --> 00:43:17.246
[dramatic music]

665
00:43:20.249 --> 00:43:26.299
[tense music]

666
00:43:31.521 --> 00:43:37.310
[Chucho snarling]
[tense music continues]

667
00:43:56.285 --> 00:43:59.419
[blade squelching]
[tense music continues]

668
00:43:59.941 --> 00:44:03.641
[Luis breathing heavily]
[somber music]

669
00:44:07.166 --> 00:44:10.648
[gentle music]
[machines beeping]

670
00:44:13.128 --> 00:44:16.654
[no audible dialogue]

671
00:44:32.060 --> 00:44:38.110
-[baby crying]
-[no audible dialogue]

672
00:44:48.686 --> 00:44:54.692
[gentle music continues]

673
00:45:00.045 --> 00:45:04.179
[upbeat Latin music]
[lively chatter]

674
00:45:13.014 --> 00:45:15.364
Feels like I finally
got my brother back.

675
00:45:17.018 --> 00:45:18.019
I'm so proud of him.

676
00:45:20.848 --> 00:45:22.850
I'm sure he's proud of you.

677
00:45:24.678 --> 00:45:28.160
You're just as responsible
as he is for things workin' out.

678
00:45:29.944 --> 00:45:31.250
for what you chose.

679
00:45:31.337 --> 00:45:35.384
[upbeat Latin music
continues faintly]

680
00:45:35.471 --> 00:45:37.256
I was thinkin' when I go back
to the Bricks

681
00:45:37.386 --> 00:45:38.736
and get things settled down...

682
00:45:41.651 --> 00:45:44.829
maybe your people and my people.
we could be in business.

683
00:45:48.528 --> 00:45:50.168
Maggie. you should bring
your people here.

684
00:45:54.229 --> 00:45:56.754
Hey. everything the Croat said
about this place is true.

685
00:45:57.493 --> 00:45:58.886
It is a fortress.

686
00:46:00.758 --> 00:46:05.806
The only thing that we are
missing is someone who knows how

687
00:46:05.893 --> 00:46:07.416
to keep things safe.

688
00:46:10.376 --> 00:46:11.943
This isn't my home.

689
00:46:13.466 --> 00:46:17.905
Why can't it be?
I'm serious. Maggie.

690
00:46:18.645 --> 00:46:22.954
Give me one good reason why
this can't be your fresh start.

691
00:46:25.130 --> 00:46:28.786
I mean. Maggie.
you and me together.

692
00:46:29.743 --> 00:46:32.746
Just imagine.

693
00:46:38.578 --> 00:46:39.927
I'll have to think about it.

694
00:46:42.408 --> 00:46:43.452
I have to talk to Hershel.

695
00:46:45.498 --> 00:46:46.498
Of course.

696
00:46:48.806 --> 00:46:50.285
Nothing's more
important than family.

697
00:46:54.550 --> 00:47:00.339
-[Negan groaning]
-[faint Latin music]

698
00:47:01.993 --> 00:47:03.953
Are you really gonna
leave without sayin' goodbye?

699
00:47:04.734 --> 00:47:05.823
Well. you know me.

700
00:47:05.953 --> 00:47:07.955
Never one
to overstay my welcome.

701
00:47:11.219 --> 00:47:12.830
Thank you.

702
00:47:14.657 --> 00:47:15.702
For what you did today.

703
00:47:17.878 --> 00:47:19.662
I wasn't sure
that I'd convince you.

704
00:47:22.840 --> 00:47:23.840
Well. you did.

705
00:47:24.798 --> 00:47:25.798
How?

706
00:47:28.846 --> 00:47:31.979
I mean. you. um...
You said you needed me.

707
00:47:34.199 --> 00:47:35.635
[Negan sighs]

708
00:47:38.246 --> 00:47:41.989
You know what happened
this morning at Ginny's grave?

709
00:47:43.904 --> 00:47:45.824
There was a lotta shit goin' on.
you know? But...

710
00:47:47.299 --> 00:47:50.041
I wasn't mad at you
for <i>tryin'</i> to kill me.

711
00:47:52.652 --> 00:47:54.828
I was mad at you
because you <i>didn't</i>.

712
00:47:57.396 --> 00:48:01.530
[somber music]
[Negan sighing]

713
00:48:01.791 --> 00:48:03.706
Why didn't you finish the job.
Maggie?

714
00:48:04.055 --> 00:48:08.450
[somber music continues]

715
00:48:08.537 --> 00:48:09.669
'Cause somewhere inside.

716
00:48:09.756 --> 00:48:11.845
I knew you were capable
of what you did today.

717
00:48:13.368 --> 00:48:14.543
You better be careful.

718
00:48:14.630 --> 00:48:16.415
You're makin' my head
get all kinds of big.

719
00:48:16.676 --> 00:48:22.029
[somber music continues]

720
00:48:22.334 --> 00:48:23.334
[chuckling]

721
00:48:24.727 --> 00:48:27.078
You know. I don't think
I've ever seen you smile.

722
00:48:28.253 --> 00:48:29.254
It suits you.

723
00:48:29.384 --> 00:48:32.213
[somber music continues]
[Negan groaning]

724
00:48:35.521 --> 00:48:38.741
Well. you need me again...

725
00:48:39.873 --> 00:48:44.704
-You know where I'll be.
-That bar? Really?

726
00:48:48.403 --> 00:48:50.275
Turns out we might not
be goin' far.

727
00:48:51.711 --> 00:48:53.452
Thinkin' about staying.

728
00:48:53.843 --> 00:48:55.410
I think Hershel
really likes it here.

729
00:48:58.718 --> 00:49:00.589
You really think
you can change it here?

730
00:49:02.504 --> 00:49:05.159
Once we find the Dama.
who's left to stop us?

731
00:49:05.290 --> 00:49:11.296
[somber music continues]

732
00:49:16.301 --> 00:49:20.653
[dramatic music]

733
00:49:53.642 --> 00:49:59.692
[tense music]
[walkers snarling]

734
00:50:06.220 --> 00:50:09.832
[dumpster rumbling]

735
00:50:10.572 --> 00:50:12.183
That's it...

736
00:50:14.489 --> 00:50:19.625
-Oh. god... Oh. god.
-[groaning]

737
00:50:20.408 --> 00:50:23.716
[walkers growling]

738
00:50:27.502 --> 00:50:28.416
Shit!

739
00:50:28.503 --> 00:50:34.509
[eerie music]

740
00:50:39.123 --> 00:50:40.733
Oh. you poor boys.

741
00:50:43.823 --> 00:50:45.042
You're hurt.

742
00:50:47.827 --> 00:50:51.178
Half of Midtown... is gone.

743
00:50:51.526 --> 00:50:55.835
-[Linus] There's no one left.
-No. There must be others.

744
00:50:57.141 --> 00:50:59.578
You'll rest. you'll heal...

745
00:50:59.839 --> 00:51:02.407
And when you're ready.
you'll help me find them.

746
00:51:03.408 --> 00:51:04.757
And then we begin again.

747
00:51:06.454 --> 00:51:09.762
Every empire starts
with the broken.

748
00:51:09.892 --> 00:51:15.985
[eerie music continues]

749
00:51:16.247 --> 00:51:20.033
Yes. our work is just beginning.

750
00:51:20.164 --> 00:51:25.604
[suspenseful music]

751
00:51:34.961 --> 00:51:36.286
This place is the start of
something else.

752
00:51:36.310 --> 00:51:37.529
something better.

753
00:51:37.616 --> 00:51:38.680
We could bring
in even more people.

754
00:51:38.704 --> 00:51:41.794
Here we go.

755
00:51:41.881 --> 00:51:44.275
The whole. you know.
New York City thing.

756
00:51:44.405 --> 00:51:45.885
it is starting to feel
like home.

757
00:51:46.059 --> 00:51:49.280
♪

758
00:51:49.410 --> 00:51:51.301
You and Renata really got
something here. Maggie.

759
00:51:51.325 --> 00:51:53.849
It's your job
to protect this place.

760
00:51:53.936 --> 00:51:56.176
This is what we asked for
when we turned on that light.

761
00:51:56.243 --> 00:52:00.639
♪

762
00:52:00.769 --> 00:52:02.336
We've come to make a deal.

763
00:52:02.467 --> 00:52:04.730
It gets in the wrong hands.
it could be dangerous.

764
00:52:04.860 --> 00:52:07.472
If you were in charge.
none of this would be happening.

765
00:52:09.038 --> 00:52:10.953
-What's going on?
-We're taking our home back.

766
00:52:12.433 --> 00:52:14.783
I'm guessing this isn't
your first suicide mission.

767
00:52:14.870 --> 00:52:16.611
Not hardly.

768
00:52:16.698 --> 00:52:17.743
Look out!

769
00:52:17.830 --> 00:52:24.402
♪

770
00:52:24.489 --> 00:52:26.273
Together. we can do something

771
00:52:26.360 --> 00:52:28.145
bigger than we've
ever done before.

772
00:52:28.232 --> 00:52:31.322
♪

773
00:52:34.194 --> 00:52:35.911
-You guys rolling?
-Yeah. I mean. I'm rolling.

774
00:52:35.935 --> 00:52:37.502
-Yeah.
-[Laughs]

775
00:52:38.242 --> 00:52:41.375
After this much time
we did a season...

776
00:52:41.506 --> 00:52:43.116
-It shocked us.
-That shocked us.

777
00:52:43.247 --> 00:52:44.857
Yeah.

778
00:52:45.031 --> 00:52:46.815
You fucking stabbed me.

779
00:52:46.946 --> 00:52:48.837
It is a one time offer with
a 10-second expiration date.

780
00:52:48.861 --> 00:52:50.602
so you better get to it.

781
00:52:50.732 --> 00:52:52.101
For the first couple
of years I was on the show.

782
00:52:52.125 --> 00:52:53.561
Lauren can hardly look at me.

783
00:52:53.735 --> 00:52:56.390
Her process as an actor. and...

784
00:52:56.521 --> 00:52:57.881
I just didn't have
my glasses on.

785
00:52:58.000 --> 00:52:59.567
Maybe didn't have
her glasses on.

786
00:52:59.698 --> 00:53:01.439
[Both grunt]

787
00:53:01.569 --> 00:53:03.528
Sorry. I thought you were
better on your feet.

788
00:53:03.658 --> 00:53:05.007
Good to see you. too.

789
00:53:05.138 --> 00:53:07.009
And then we started
this spin off.

790
00:53:07.184 --> 00:53:09.142
Every scene.
it was always so heavy.

791
00:53:09.273 --> 00:53:11.797
There was never a lightness
or a humor to it.

792
00:53:11.927 --> 00:53:14.974
We are quite silly people
in a very dark world.

793
00:53:15.104 --> 00:53:16.932
-And now it's...
-And now we...

794
00:53:17.063 --> 00:53:18.519
-we can do it.
-We get to bring that

795
00:53:18.543 --> 00:53:19.979
in front of the camera.

796
00:53:20.153 --> 00:53:23.287
I'm going to flip
you around like this.

797
00:53:23.461 --> 00:53:26.464
and you're gonna fucking
Bruce Lee the fuck out of them.

798
00:53:26.594 --> 00:53:29.249
[Laughs]
I'm no help.

799
00:53:29.423 --> 00:53:31.773
In this season.
they actually work together.

800
00:53:31.947 --> 00:53:33.645
Heard you call him Negan.

801
00:53:33.775 --> 00:53:37.605
Rumor has it that's the name
of the Croat's number two.

802
00:53:37.779 --> 00:53:40.042
Maggy and Negan are zip tied
together. and there we go.

803
00:53:40.173 --> 00:53:41.613
-Yeah. and you never see us...
-No.

804
00:53:41.696 --> 00:53:43.524
Under other people's control.

805
00:53:43.655 --> 00:53:44.980
They're at it with each other.
but this was

806
00:53:45.004 --> 00:53:47.136
a great way of us being joined

807
00:53:47.311 --> 00:53:49.095
in misery against another force.

808
00:53:49.226 --> 00:53:50.706
-Yeah.
-Let's talk about this scene.

809
00:53:50.792 --> 00:53:51.967
We need to find cover.

810
00:53:52.098 --> 00:53:53.839
We need to find Negan.

811
00:53:53.969 --> 00:53:56.233
One of the cellar doors
leading to the street is open.

812
00:53:56.363 --> 00:53:58.278
Beneath the open door.
makeshift slide.

813
00:53:58.409 --> 00:54:01.150
A beat later. Maggie.
Negan tumble down the slide.

814
00:54:01.281 --> 00:54:03.240
-[Grunts]
-[Grunts]

815
00:54:03.370 --> 00:54:04.719
The walkers immediately on them.

816
00:54:04.850 --> 00:54:06.480
That was a cool sequence
that was sort of

817
00:54:06.504 --> 00:54:08.177
still being worked out
closer to production.

818
00:54:08.201 --> 00:54:10.421
-It got worked out on the day.
-That too.

819
00:54:10.551 --> 00:54:11.813
[Both laugh]

820
00:54:11.944 --> 00:54:12.945
You were being so nice.

821
00:54:21.780 --> 00:54:23.608
[Laughter]

822
00:54:23.738 --> 00:54:25.629
Originally it's a fight
in the streets. remember?

823
00:54:25.653 --> 00:54:27.533
-And it was the dust.
-You had an eye infection.

824
00:54:27.568 --> 00:54:29.111
-I had an eye infection.
-I had a nose.

825
00:54:29.135 --> 00:54:30.417
-a sinus infection.
-Yeah. and we were...

826
00:54:30.441 --> 00:54:32.443
So we couldn't do the
super dusty scene.

827
00:54:32.573 --> 00:54:34.358
We were both like.
"We'll die. you know?"

828
00:54:34.488 --> 00:54:36.098
-Yeah.
-My eye is going to fall

829
00:54:36.229 --> 00:54:37.772
out of my head.
and she's just gonna die.

830
00:54:37.796 --> 00:54:39.469
Yeah. and my nose
was going into my face.

831
00:54:39.493 --> 00:54:41.321
I know we seem
like superheroes. but...

832
00:54:41.452 --> 00:54:43.410
No. just kidding.
[Laughs]

833
00:54:43.541 --> 00:54:46.152
I mean. I believe us for
what it's worth working together

834
00:54:46.326 --> 00:54:49.286
that I'm here doing this.
and then Negan comes in.

835
00:54:49.416 --> 00:54:50.896
I'm sorry for this.

836
00:54:51.026 --> 00:54:53.725
-For what?
-[Walkers growling]

837
00:54:53.899 --> 00:54:55.857
[Grunts] [Walker crashing

838
00:54:55.988 --> 00:54:57.990
And cut.
Good.

839
00:54:58.120 --> 00:54:59.881
It's the first time we've
seen them really fight together

840
00:54:59.905 --> 00:55:02.516
since season... yeah.

841
00:55:02.690 --> 00:55:04.126
It could have been 11.

842
00:55:04.301 --> 00:55:07.304
-We need numbers. please.
-We need you.

843
00:55:07.434 --> 00:55:09.393
I need you.

844
00:55:09.523 --> 00:55:11.153
I think what sets
the whole thing in motion.

845
00:55:11.177 --> 00:55:14.311
of being able to move forward
is. for herself and for her son.

846
00:55:14.441 --> 00:55:17.139
there has to be a life
without anger.

847
00:55:17.270 --> 00:55:19.185
There has to be a moving
forward.

848
00:55:19.316 --> 00:55:21.796
The possibilities
for this new world

849
00:55:21.927 --> 00:55:23.972
and for us are tremendous.

850
00:55:24.103 --> 00:55:25.670
I really should have
stabbed you.

851
00:55:25.800 --> 00:55:27.454
You weren't gonna stab me.

852
00:55:27.585 --> 00:55:29.265
Oh. I was so gonna
stab you a little bit.

853
00:55:29.326 --> 00:55:33.330
♪

854
00:55:35.157 --> 00:55:41.033
[outro music]
